- op: discuss  # e80d
  at: '2026-08-11T08:25:43Z'  # e80d
  by: agent  # e80d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e80d
  clock: 7  # e80d
  nonce: e80d  # e80d
  message: "REOPENED: satisfied for the INSTALL entry points only; the RUNTIME ones carry the\nidentical defect and were never in scope.\n\nThis item's statement is the exact rule being broken -- \"every entry point with an\nasserted 'no direct host_fs writes' claim must route every fs-write primitive\n(write_text, mkdir, unlink, chmod, copy2, rmtree, replace) through a safety_zones.py\nwrapper.\" The 2026-05-23 closure covered build_grammars.py and gitleaks.py, i.e. the\ncmd_build_grammars / cmd_install_gitleaks entry points. runtime-cli-no-host-fs is\nalso an asserted no-direct-host_fs claim, and it has eight unwrapped call sites.\n\nFOUND BY HAND (grep over core src for the 40 catalogued python fs_write primitives,\nexcluding safety_zones.py and the install/build modules) AND INDEPENDENTLY BY THE\nTOOL (verify-claims on dev 528a7e5bcb reports runtime-cli-no-host-fs violated with\n35 DISTINCT flows: 10 mkdir + 1 rmtree + 24 builtins.open). The two agree on the\nreal set; the 24 open rows are a separate false-positive defect (WI-rusof).\n\n  cli.py:1033   cmd_sketch          shutil.rmtree   -- tmp_artifact_rmtree EXISTS, unused\n  cli.py:1450   _handle_files_mode  Path.mkdir      -- no user_out_mkdir wrapper\n  cli.py:1942   cmd_slice           Path.mkdir      -- ditto\n  cli.py:4490   cmd_compact         Path.mkdir      -- ditto\n  cli.py:9451   _emit_handler_slices Path.mkdir     -- ditto\n  cli.py:10227  run_survey          Path.mkdir      -- ditto\n  sketch_embeddings.py:1431/1472    Path.mkdir      -- cache_mkdir EXISTS, unused\n\nFOUR OF THE FIVE cli.py mkdir calls sit on the line DIRECTLY ABOVE a\nuser_out_write / user_out_open_json_dump call: the write is wrapped and the mkdir\nthat creates its directory is not. safety_zones.py has cache_mkdir,\ntmp_artifact_mkdir and install_artifact_mkdir but no user_out_mkdir -- the zone\nthat takes a USER-SUPPLIED path is the one zone with no mkdir wrapper.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE (not a proxy metric): on a two-file scratch repo,\n  python3 -m hypergumbo_core survey . --out <TMP>/ARBITRARY/deep/nested/tree/map.json\ncreated ARBITRARY/, deep/, nested/ and tree/ -- four levels at a caller-chosen path\noutside every declared zone -- and wrote map.64k.json, map.16k.json, map.4k.json and\nmap.slices/ that the user never named.\n\nFIX: add user_out_mkdir, migrate the eight call sites, register it as a sanitizer in\nthe user_out sink catalog (same three-step shape the 2026-05-23 fix used for\ntmp_artifact_mkdir / install_artifact_mkdir)."  # e80d
